C o m p i l a t i o n


      CEE 6410 - Engineering Systems Analysis
       
      Formulate and solve the PRIMAL and DUALs of THE PROBLEM:
       
      An aqueduct has excess capacity in the months of June, July, & August.
        Hay or grain can be planted over a max of 10000 acres. Data are as follows:
       
                              Hay        Grain
      June                    2          1            14000 acft
      July                    1          2            18000 acft
      August                  1          0             6000 acft
      Land                    1          1            10000 acre
      Return, $/acre          $100       $120
       
          Determine the optimal planting for the two crops.
       
      THE SOLUTION:
      Uses General Algebraic Modeling System to Solve this Linear Program
       
      Samuel Torgersen-Gonzalez
      s.torgersen-gonzalez@usu.edu
      1 October 2026
  25   
  26  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  27  SETS plnt crops growing /Hay, Grain/
  28       mnth months /June, July, August, Land/;
  29   
  30  * 2. DEFINE input data
  31  PARAMETERS
  32     c(plnt) Objective function coefficients ($ per acre)
  33           /Hay   100,
  34            Grain 120/
  35     b(mnth) Right hand constraint values (acft per month)
  36            /June   14000,
  37             July   18000,
  38             August  6000
  39             Land   10000/;
  40   
  41  TABLE A(plnt,mnth) Left hand side constraint coefficients
  42              June  July  August  Land
  43   Hay        2     1     1       1
  44   Grain      1     2     0       1     ;
  45   
  46  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  47  VARIABLES X(plnt)  crop planted (acft)
  48            VPROFIT  total profit ($)
  49            Y(mnth)  value of months used (units specific to variable)
  50            VREDCOST total reduced cost ($);
  51   
  52  * Non-negativity constraints
  53  POSITIVE VARIABLES X,Y;
  54   
  55  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  56  EQUATIONS
  57     PROFIT_PRIMAL Total benefit ($) and objective function value
  58     RES_CONS_PRIMAL(mnth) Month constraints
  59     REDCOST_DUAL Reduced benefit ($) associated with using months
  60     RES_CONS_DUAL(plnt) Profit levels ;
  61   
  62  *Primal Equations
  63  PROFIT_PRIMAL..                 VPROFIT =E= SUM(plnt,c(plnt)*X(plnt));
  64  RES_CONS_PRIMAL(mnth) ..    SUM(plnt,A(plnt,mnth)*X(plnt)) =L= b(mnth);
  65   
  66  *Dual Equations
  67  REDCOST_DUAL..                 VREDCOST =E= SUM(mnth,b(mnth)*Y(mnth));
  68  RES_CONS_DUAL(plnt)..          sum(mnth,A(plnt,mnth)*Y(mnth)) =G= c(plnt);
  69   
  70  X.LO(plnt) = 5;
  71   
  72  * 5. DEFINE the MODELS
  73  *PRIMAL model
  74  MODEL PLANT_PRIMAL /PROFIT_PRIMAL, RES_CONS_PRIMAL/;
  75  *Set the options file to print out range of basis information
  76  PLANT_PRIMAL.optfile = 1;
  77   
  78  *DUAL model
  79  MODEL PLANT_DUAL /REDCOST_DUAL, RES_CONS_DUAL/;
  80   
  81  * 6. SOLVE the MODELS
  82  * Solve the PLANTING PRIMAL model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  83  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  84  SOLVE PLANT_PRIMAL USING LP MAXIMIZING VPROFIT;
  85   
  86  * Solve the PLANTING DUAL model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  87  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  88  SOLVE PLANT_DUAL USING LP MINIMIZING VREDCOST;
  89  *Order does not matter!
  90   
  91  * 6. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file
  92   
  93  * 7 . Dump all data and results to GAMS proprietary file storage .gdx and to Excel
  94  Execute_Unload "Ex2-1Dual.gdx";
  95  * Dump the gdx file to an Excel workbook
  96  Execute "gdx2xls Ex2-1Dual.gdx"
  97  * To open the GDX file in the GAMS IDE, select File => Open.
  98  * In the Open window, set Filetype to .gdx and select the file.


